Fix five shell harness runs that fail on jusprin-dev

Five runs of the shell test app (--print-issues, --print-issue-readers,
--printer-network-check, --printer-connect-skill and
--project-prompt-requests) failed on every try. Four had checks that later
commits made stale; one found a real app bug.

- The print-issue and printer-chat runs send a second message in one chat.
  Since 6b59a887ca a chat keeps its provider, and that message fails when
  no key is stored for it. 084b8d35a7 gave only the default run's mock AI a
  key; these runs now get one too.
- The network check's Moonraker case still called the Bambu connect tool,
  which 83a8431df2 split off. It now calls printer_host_connect.
- The OrcaSlicer 2.5.0 merge (975c703f08) brought the Bambu Lab profile
  sync (upstream edc2f8bf90a). Presets are now per nozzle, and TPU 95A HF
  is no longer limited to the H2D's right nozzle. The readers run picks
  the new presets and uses TPU 85A, which keeps that limit.
- Since upstream 81357695c5 a prime tower partly off the plate is a
  validation error and OrcaSlicer will not slice. The readers run now
  checks that the print-issue monitor blocks in OrcaSlicer's words, and
  the step that sliced with that tower is gone. No step now produces
  OrcaSlicer's nozzle-area warning on a slice.
- App bug: OrcaSlicer 2.5.0 (upstream 514ab02525) reworded "A G-code path
  goes beyond the plate boundaries." to "...beyond plate boundaries.", and
  the monitor kept the old sentence, so it no longer matched. The monitor,
  the print-issues skill's quote, its tests and the recorded prompt
  requests use the new words. The old entry is removed by hand from the
  JusPrin native catalogs, not by a full regeneration, because those
  catalogs were already stale from 3c134d39e3.
